{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564144-house-ruling-gargoyles-v20","id":1564144,"title":"House ruling Gargoyles [V20]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-09-17T12:24:36-07:00","id":1564144,"title":"House ruling Gargoyles [V20]","content":"I recently made a Gargoyle NPC under V20 rules and noticed how dissatisfied I was with the way their variants/Discipline spread works. Combined with their severe Bloodline flaws and the somewhat underwhelming Visceratika as a Protean variant, I want to house rule some of that for my games.<br /> <br /> Thematically, I liked the Dark Ages approach of deconstructing the Disciplines into powers and enchantments, as that was fitting for them as a half-construct. However, for a modern Bloodline, it's pretty convoluted (and expensive; 10 XP per dot is silly).<br /> As a test, I made a Caitiff with the Monstrous, Weak Willed, and Amnesia flaws. That was more than enough to give them the Additional Discipline merit for Flight.<br /> <br /> What I think I will do is get rid of Visceratika and let them be able to pick Disciplines from their 'parent' Clans + Flight at Caitiff costs, with Auspex, Obfuscate, and Protean as suggested defaults. Visceratika 2 is an easy alternative power for Auspex 2, and Protean 4 can be Horrid Form from Vicissitude instead of Shape of the Beast.<br /> <br /> Also, instead of the Weak Willed variant as a Bloodline flaw, I think I will change that to the Dark Statue power but as a disadvantage: At dawn they turn to unconscious stone, regardless of whether they are outside or not, and are completely immobile. So the Disney Gargoyle flaw, just because I really like that.<br /> <br /> Having said all that, I'm pretty sure I'm not alone with house ruling modern Gargoyle variants, and I would be interested in what others have done with them. IMO as written, they are difficult picks for PC characters, and lack a bit of appeal in 'being' Gargoyles aside from Flight and the looks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-17T15:27:52-07:00","id":1564145,"title":"","content":"IIRC, my group decided something along the same lines about 20 yrs ago. We went with Potence, Fortitude, and a modified Protean as bloodline disciplines and a weakness of perpetually cold hard skin. (Their Protean was, IIRC - I don\u2019t know what happened to my old notes - the same night vision and claws, a third tier power I\u2019m blanking on, growing wings instead of becoming a bat/wolf, and turning to stone instead of mist/fog.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-17T22:51:53-07:00","id":1564157,"title":"","content":"I'm bothered by their Weak Willed weakness, but not by Visceratika.<br /> <br /> The thing is, this is not a Protean variant at all. It's a Castle Guardian power, a very consistent one:<br /> <br /> Skin of the Chameleon give you +5 Stealth and you don't have much reason to run within a building. For mobile surveillance it's better than Obfuscate 1.<br /> <br /> Scry the Hearthstone gives you direct information about everyone in the building at once. Bond with the Mountain works on stone, and as the level five power clarifies, also with concrete and cement, possibly other similar materials (clay, ceramic, plaster, asphalt?)<br /> <br /> Armor of Terra is a nice set of minor bonuses until you notice it halves every fire damage dice pool before soak. Flow Within the Mountain is a free pass into any building on top of almost undetectable stealth as you're completely out of sight, and is not an Elder Level.<br /> <br /> Together they make for a very effective means to control and move through your own Haven, and guard or invade any building. The fact its stone-melding effects work on city ground make them way more useful than Earth Meld, and even more depending on the city or if you convince the ST to include plaster.<br /> <br /> Would I, as ST, include plaster? Yes. Not only is it thematically close to concrete and other building materials, plenty of cities around the world, in rich and poor countries alike, use a lot more stone and concrete to build than the US, so this power already works in walls in actually most of the world. I don't see a need to let the US be the snowflake and diminish the potential of this. You already pay the price by making it obvious to everyone you have Visceratika (as you turn grey at level 4 if you're not a Gargoyle).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-18T02:53:11-07:00","id":1564164,"title":"","content":"Visceratika is pretty good for what it is meant to do, ie provide the tools a guard needs. In Dark Ages the powers work fine, but in a modern setting I would say stealth alone isn't sufficient for a character with the Monstrous flaw. It's <i>possible</i> to play one without Obfuscate, but in a crowded city it can make things awkward especially when moving about with the Coterie. I know nobody looks up in cities, but social interactions with mortals (something Dark Ages Gargoyles weren't even expected to have, as opposed to Nosferatu) become almost completely impossible.<br /> <br /> There's also that the stealth and awareness aspects of Visceratika don't scale. The Scouts who need to be out and about have both Auspex and Obfuscate, and I think that's more fitting for an independent Bloodline no longer tied to their ancestral purpose - more for gameplay reasons than canon ones, though. I wouldn't even mind putting Visceratika on top of those, but if you add Protean in the mix it does become rather redundant. Still, no reason to not make it at least optional.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Earth Meld for Gargoyles should absolutely work on stone and 'city materials' instead of soil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T07:11:36-07:00","id":1564190,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate uses Stealth rolls. Skin of the Chameleon is a considerable boost, especially against pesky Auspex users.<br /> <br /> Scry the Heartstone gives a blank statement Auspex can't provide, but can explore. It's not doing the same thing, Auspex is the best for an immediate area, but this is a complete scan on the whole building that includes how many are Obfuscated within.<br /> <br /> Armor of Terra is still halving fire before soak. It effectively doubles anything you have for soak against fire, on top of being a Fortitude dot that adds to Fortitude itself.<br /> <br /> I really think this is plenty of synergy between powers and that you're greatly underestimating how Visceratika can be used outside being a guard, <i><b>especially</b></i> in a modern city.<br /> <br /> During the Dark Ages it gave you awareness in a castle or temple. In a modern city it can give you a few floors in an apartment or office building at once, the immediate layout of any facility, a way in and out of vaults and locked rooms. Almost everything around you is rock or cement, almost everything happens inside buildings, and beneath everything there is a lot of infrastructure that you can use.<br /> <br /> But for this same reason, I would not give this access to rock to Protean. Not only are the metaphysical rationales distinct, the change in usefulness is substantial.<br /> <br /> You can add other Disciplines to their spread, I think the second Weakness is severe enough to justify and Flight is useful, but lackluster IMO. But I really wouldn't cut Visceratika even as a player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T17:43:35-07:00","id":1564198,"title":"","content":"Having found a few of my older notes, our alternate Gargoyle power was at one point: 1) night vision, 2) claws that also made climbing easier, 3) stone skin (similar to the revised era Serpentis power), 4) wings/flight, and the ability to physically merge with one's haven or claimed location (something we took from a Requiem power called Domus). <br /> <br /> Also we used Requiem's concept of Devotions, with the Gargoyles having developed (instinctually or otherwise) a number of ones that duplicated Skin of the Chameleon, Voice of the Castle, Rockheart, and some of the powers from Requiem's Domus and Tenure disciplines. <br /> <br /> Not that this is necessarily the ideal version of the bloodline and its discipline, but for our purposes it worked relatively well IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T00:16:20-07:00","id":1564209,"title":"","content":"This surprises me.<br /> <br /> I recently played a Gargoyle and was surprised by how well their kit worked. Not only was it strong, their powers fit with their lore quite a lot.<br /> <br /> They are a bit St dependent, the st needs to let a monstrous kindred function without obfuscate. Gargoyles look like monsters and have wings. The st we played with let me wrap up in a bandaged face and rags and pretend at being a burn victim. Wings could be wrapped up back and hidden somewhat. There also wasn't constant rolls to move in the city. Without that it'd be too inconvenient to run the bloodline.<br /> <br /> The second drawback is they want a lot of disciplines. They only need Visceratika 2 and flight 1 but they really want as much as possible.<br /> <br /> The third is they can't carry much with them.<br /> Their stealth ability, Visceratika 1, requires them to be naked.<br /> Flight needs a lot of dots before you can carry a lot with you <br /> <br /> Given those drawbacks you have some extreme strength, the biggest one being synergy.<br /> All the V20 gargoyle powers fit into each other.<br /> They all let you do what gargoyles were made for: guard domains, invade domains, scout, fight.<br /> <br /> Visceratika is really good here.<br /> It's thematic, all its powers hint at the parent clan powers. I like that a lot more than them just having the original disciplines outright.<br /> <br /> It's also so very useful. You have a strong stealth ability, a strong scry ability that massively boosts stealth, a sleep safe ability that along with flight makes it trivial for you to stay outside (keep scouting, investigate a place to dawn), an extra boost to fortitude that also makes you fire resistant, and a way to make it even easier for you to get into some places.<br /> <br /> Beyond that potence is great on its own and greater for a stealth stabber, fortitude is useful especially if you aren't carrying armor and flight makes it even easier for you to get into buildings.<br /> <br /> Protean 2 would be great for them. The eyes almost more than the claws.<br /> <br /> But all in their kit really help them in their given role and most of their powers lock into each other. And it fits with their lore, feels really elegant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T04:48:43-07:00","id":1564213,"title":"","content":"I'm increasingly of the opinion that Flight and Visceratika should be folded together, for a few reasons.<br /> <br /> - 3 disciplines is the norm<br /> - Gargoyles have a lot of downsides to them, so Visceratika being an extremely good Discipline is fine in my view!<br /> - it makes learning &quot;Flight&quot; come as a package with learning Visceratika, and learning Visceratika means getting a stony hue to your skin and sprouting wings, at least in my view!<br /> <br /> The net result of this is that Gargoyles can realistically exist without Obfuscate, since their mobility Discipline and their Stealth Discipline are tied together. You're sorta stuck being a naked weirdo who travels from rooftop to rooftop, descending into Elysia through agreed vertical entrances, but that fits very neatly into the fantasy of the Gargoyle. And if you want to eschew the Gargoyle Archetype, as a Gargoyle, you can always learn Obfuscate 3 and start wearing clothes!<br /> <br /> I am also not a fan of Gargoyles having Appearance 0. I think it makes sense that many of them do, but ultimately their Curse should be &quot;You look like a Gargoyle! Big stone guy with wings!&quot; with a side helping of &quot;You're easy to enslave&quot;, &quot;You don't have a Primogen&quot;, &quot;You're a social creature who suffers penalties if you're alone in the world, no master, no allies etc.&quot; and all the social stuff that comes with it. I played a DAV20 Gargoyle who wound up with Appearance 6 (via Vicissitude), as it happens! It's worth noting that Nosferatu's Clan Curse mentions that Appearance is stuck at 0, while none of the Gargoyle ones do, so you can alter their Appearance score with Vicissitude, RAW!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T06:22:36-07:00","id":1564214,"title":"","content":"Hm, the more I read here, the more I think just giving players access to the pool of 'ancestral' Disciplines + Visceratika at Caitff costs is the easiest compromise. That way they have the options to adjust their Disciplines to their character at creation and moving forward. Animalism isn't a bad fit for Gargoyles imo, but Vicissitude would be a bit of an outlier. Maybe a variant that works on stone and steel instead of flesh and bone could be interesting? Visceratika used to have Level 6 power for animating stone. Or just exclude it from the pool.<br /> <br /> The alternative would be to go with the standard spread and cherrypick thematically suitable levels from that list as available powers, Dark Ages style. Since most of them are in the lower ranges of the Discipline anyway, I think that would just complicate things unnecessarily though.<br /> <br /> For Flight, I considered making it an Ability instead of a Discipline. I don't like the idea of locking it behind a specific Discipline level since Flight is a signature ability for Gargoyles, so folding it into Visceratika is an attractive alternative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T10:02:24-07:00","id":1564215,"title":"","content":"A really good thing for gargoyles outside of disciplines is to have some backing. It really helps if they're a respected operative of some larger group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T11:05:53-07:00","id":1564218,"title":"","content":"Folding both Flight and stony appearance into Visceratika is probably a good idea. Instead of a clan with extra Weakness in exchange for a 4th Discipline, a Discipline with built-in weakness to compensate an extra effect.<br /> <br /> Agree with giving it a better mechanical effect than Appearance 0. Declare it Obvious Appearance or something (always look supernatural, even disguised is bulky and remarkable, you can say you're in cosplay or a body modification freak, but never be discreet). If needed add the penalty to touch from Armor of Terra.<br /> <br /> I don't think giving access to ancestor Disciplines is a good idea. Goes against every other Bloodline. Gargoyles aren't unique in how they came to be, no one else does that. And if it is done, any exception will look too arbitrary even if you don't picture a Gargoyle fleshcrafting. I'd go with the folding and call it a day.<br /> <br /> Still I'd look for an alternative Weakness, maybe even the Disney one, maybe something else, but the weak willed is too broad and unsatisfying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-25T14:05:49-07:00","id":1564342,"title":"","content":"OK, now I am trying to formalize it, but I'm trying to chose a new Weakness.<br /> <br /> Basically I eliminated both Weaknesses. The appearance went to Visceratika itself, the Weak Willed is just gone.<br /> <br /> In Visceratika, the Weakness is Remarkable Silhouette: your bulk is such that you always stand out. It doesn't affect the Masquerade or your Appearance rating, you can have fantastic beauty, and you can give any lame excuse to be big and grey with hard skin. You can cover yourself in a trenchcoat and will still look like a burly sore thumb in the crowd that people will remember for weeks. You're not just easy to remember and identify, you're a reference point as in &quot;follow the street, turn left on the giant freak&quot;.<br /> <br /> For the actual Gargoyle Weakness, some rough ideas, I can flesh out anything I actually decide upon:<br /> <br /> 1. Uncontrolled Memory<br /> The Gargoyle can't remember its past, but it is still there. Sometimes something act as a reminder, but since it comes without context the Gargoyle is left with shock, confusion and unusual feelings without much to do about it. This may or may not include the possibility of rebuilding the past even centuries after the fact.<br /> <br /> 2. Identity Uncertainty<br /> The amnesia effect is ongoing, sometimes the Gargoyle suffers a partial memory loss, but in a specific way the Tremere engineered long ago, they remember events but forget their own role in them. The Gargoyle's memory becomes a tangle of scenes where it can be anyone, and only others can offer any anchoring.<br /> <br /> 3. Bestial Features<br /> Add to Visceratika, so I'm thinking on exploring it a little differently, as disabilities. The features are visually subtle (until Visceratika), and have no sufficient development to concede benefits (unless bought separately), but they cause actual limitation. Wings that don't unfold get tangled and limit space, a muzzle makes speech and feeding awkward, clothes must be tailored or they don't fit and degrade fast. All in all, they need adaptations to live comfortably, or even functionally, and being stranded from their accessibility tools is painful or dangerous.<br /> <br /> 4. Disney Gargoyles<br /> Because why not. Turn to stone during the day, if not enough make this stone no more resilient than the normal state. It's a very soft stone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T04:31:30-07:00","id":1564349,"title":"","content":"Something I considered as alternative Flaw was pretty much the inverse of being memorable, ie. a pseudo-Delirium effect that makes people forget the character. Maybe even going as far as something like a bad Arcane Background, which would make maintaining other Backgrounds and relations harder. It could be connected to the Amnesia and a legacy of Tremere sorcery - while the Dark Ages warlocks didn't give much of a toss about the Masquerade, some of the stealth Enchantments might have had that as a side effect.<br /> <br /> IIRC the books are also inconsistent about Appearance. <i>House of Tremere</i> had Virstania create a few Gargoyles that were described as very beautiful, so nixing Monstrous is something in line with that. Maybe that trait makes more sense as a Bloodline specific Merit, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T05:15:19-07:00","id":1564353,"title":"","content":"I imagine Visceratika becoming a means to justify vamps with mythological appearance, like Hindu gods and stuff. No need to work outside regular Appearance ratings for that, just assume that any &quot;excess&quot; in the description is offset by the impact of weirdness combined with posture. We could even have multiple wings, as long as they're functionally the same as two.<br /> <br /> Justifying bizarre appearance really isn't hard. From weird conditions to surgical modifications we can go a long way, the char just has to count on the very reliable reaction from people of assuming it has a mundane explanation. And it isn't even a lie, the character is, indeed, physically human but with a severe skin condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T08:28:44-07:00","id":1564356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564144-house-ruling-gargoyles-v20?p=1564349#post1564349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I considered as alternative Flaw was pretty much the inverse of being memorable, ie. a pseudo-Delirium effect that makes people forget the character. Maybe even going as far as something like a bad Arcane Background, which would make maintaining other Backgrounds and relations harder. It could be connected to the Amnesia and a legacy of Tremere sorcery - while the Dark Ages warlocks didn't give much of a toss about the Masquerade, some of the stealth Enchantments might have had that as a side effect.<br /> <br /> IIRC the books are also inconsistent about Appearance. <i>House of Tremere</i> had Virstania create a few Gargoyles that were described as very beautiful, so nixing Monstrous is something in line with that. Maybe that trait makes more sense as a Bloodline specific Merit, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does feel thematic for gargoyles to fade into the background. Don't think you need more of an explanation than 'strange blood sorcery side effects'. Not sure what it'd mean systemwide, cap certain backgrounds to 3? Something else?<br /> <br /> I tend to take App 0 as 'can't pass for human' though. Can be hideous or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T12:02:36-07:00","id":1564366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564144-house-ruling-gargoyles-v20?p=1564356#post1564356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to take App 0 as 'can't pass for human' though. Can be hideous or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is, what &quot;can't pass for human&quot; means?<br /> <br /> Search the internet for &quot;body modification&quot; and you'll see a lot of very interesting real life human bodies that would easy fit the description of a Gargoyle.<br /> <br /> I can give a pass to the Nos because they have a whole schtick about specifically being repulsive in any way possible, but Gargoyles aren't that.<br /> <br /> My opinion is that they don't need either to be Masquerade breaches or Appearance 0. They are weird as fuck, but that's not supernatural in itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-28T23:03:49-07:00","id":1564407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>twig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564144-house-ruling-gargoyles-v20?p=1564213#post1564213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm increasingly of the opinion that Flight and Visceratika should be folded together, for a few reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC they were actually originally (I think it was in 2nd edition) one discipline, and only got spilt in two disciplines in revised.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-29T02:47:39-07:00","id":1564414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564144-house-ruling-gargoyles-v20?p=1564407#post1564407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC they were actually originally (I think it was in 2nd edition) one discipline, and only got spilt in two disciplines in revised.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yep! I'd be happy to put it back to that, absolutely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-30T15:19:16-07:00","id":1564437,"title":"","content":"A thought has occurred to me: If any of the Gargoyles ever decided to join the Sabbat, that would be a catastrophe.<br /> <br /> You can kiss both the Masquerade and the Camarilla goodbye, when the next batch of Shovelheads results in the creation of 5 stone giants, desperate for blood, and possessing the innate ability to fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-30T21:56:50-07:00","id":1564443,"title":"","content":"Considering everything other Sabbat vampire can already do, it wouldn't be nearly as bad as it seems. In fact it wouldn't be any worse. What is a flying thing like that if not a weird big bird or an UFO. Would hardly be the only strange thing people see in the night sky.<br /> <br /> And there's probably already some in the Sabbat anyway, I'd bet there would be Gargoyles included since the beginning of the sect, all things considered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-01T02:55:21-07:00","id":1564449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564144-house-ruling-gargoyles-v20?p=1564437#post1564437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thought has occurred to me: If any of the Gargoyles ever decided to join the Sabbat, that would be a catastrophe.<br /> <br /> You can kiss both the Masquerade and the Camarilla goodbye, when the next batch of Shovelheads results in the creation of 5 stone giants, desperate for blood, and possessing the innate ability to fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's like Tuesday for the masquerade maintenance coterie. Dominate the locals, leave digital traces to the technocrats to manage, tip of Leopold to get them hunted down for you, cry to your ghoul about your job.<br /> <br /> Local news broadcast crack jokes about real life gargoyles sighting same evening 'none that looks like desdemona, wouldn't mind one like that ', 'Frakes unaivable for comment' then get some real idiot to swear 'it's real it's all real' so people can laugh at him. <br /> <br /> Gargoyles are not necessarily larger or heavier than a normal kindred though. Believe they are vitae and decayed organs underneath the stoney skin same as other kindred.<br /> <br /> Just their wings get larger the more they have in flight. <br /> <br /> And the vtm: bloodlines gargoyle was a stony giant solid statue guy without wings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-01T05:48:08-07:00","id":1564452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564144-house-ruling-gargoyles-v20?p=1564449#post1564449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gargoyles are not necessarily larger or heavier than a normal kindred though. Believe they are vitae and decayed organs underneath the stoney skin same as other kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think their mass <i>does </i>increase. At least in <i>Dark Ages</i>, there was an Enchantment specifically to reduce their weight so they don't crash through wooden floors when having a rough landing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564144-house-ruling-gargoyles-v20?p=1564443#post1564443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there's probably already some in the Sabbat anyway, I'd bet there would be Gargoyles included since the beginning of the sect, all things considered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Goratrix definitely had the means to create new Gargoyles, and even experimented with adding new Clans into the mix. The apparent lack of Gargoyles in the Sabbat could be a politics issue in which the Tzimisce weren't too keen on the Tremere <i>antitribu </i>creating new ones, and aimed at having some kind of supervision in it. That could have been one of the motivations to create the Blood Brothers. Still, I imagine some of the rebel Gargoyles must have found their way into Sabbat ranks as you say.<br /> <br /> It's interesting that the Tzimisce historically seemed to have been very careful to avoid taking their own constructs to the next step. I don't recall any Embraced szlachta, and vozhd were deliberately made from mindless ghouls. The only thing that 'integrated' other vampires I can recall was the Cathedral of Flesh, which iirc even has the word &quot;diablerized&quot; in the text after absorbing vampires.<br /> <br /> I would assume there are more than a few Caitiff that are the result of a Metamorphosist's experiments. Still interesting that no other monstrous bloodlines appeared from that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-01T14:53:04-07:00","id":1564459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564144-house-ruling-gargoyles-v20?p=1564449#post1564449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And the vtm: bloodlines gargoyle was a stony giant solid statue guy without wings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm almost certain that it's explained the wings of the Gargoyle are decorative, rather than functional. Their ability to fly is magical in nature, with the wings being too small and weak to actually sustain the body in flight.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, 10 foot tall, flying giant, crashing down in the middle of Hollywood!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-02T03:32:29-07:00","id":1564470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564144-house-ruling-gargoyles-v20?p=1564459#post1564459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm almost certain that it's explained the wings of the Gargoyle are decorative, rather than functional. Their ability to fly is magical in nature, with the wings being too small and weak to actually sustain the body in flight.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, 10 foot tall, flying giant, crashing down in the middle of Hollywood!</div> </div> </div> </div>Huge merit well spent.<br /> <br /> I looked into v20 but couldn't find anything about size or weight so it's either a random line missed or one of those undefined things you have to think about what makes sense or what's the coolest.<br /> <br /> Alternatively have voidshaper make their flaw so that gargoyles get larger and stonier the older they get or the more they rotshreck. 10 ft invisible flying statues all around us.<br /> <br /> V20 did mention tzimisci base gargoyles look 'fleshy'. Nosferatu base looks hideous(but also they all do) and gangrel look 'feral'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-02T07:21:05-07:00","id":1564481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564144-house-ruling-gargoyles-v20?p=1564470#post1564470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huge merit well spent.<br /> <br /> I looked into v20 but couldn't find anything about size or weight so it's either a random line missed or one of those undefined things you have to think about what makes sense or what's the coolest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do vaguely recall reading something about a discipline that causes the vampire to alter their body mass, but I can't remember the the specifics about it. I came across it years ago, so the details are hazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-02T23:51:35-07:00","id":1564498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564144-house-ruling-gargoyles-v20?p=1564481#post1564481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do vaguely recall reading something about a discipline that causes the vampire to alter their body mass, but I can't remember the the specifics about it. I came across it years ago, so the details are hazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I saw it once, but wasn't Visceratika, it was some Caitiff who developed it or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-03T11:52:54-07:00","id":1564510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564144-house-ruling-gargoyles-v20?p=1564498#post1564498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I saw it once, but wasn't Visceratika, it was some Caitiff who developed it or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, that was it!<br /> <br /> <b>Glide</b>, one of the Thinblood powers for the original build of Bloodlines 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-09T04:09:19-07:00","id":1564634,"title":"","content":"So, there is at least one canonical Gargoyle in the Sabbat: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Erinyi\" target=\"_blank\">Erinyi</a>. She's also fairly pretty, as far as Gargoyles go (at least according to the artwork).<br /> <br /> Personally, I've always been tempted to go with <i>Exalted</i> 3e's version of Appearance, where a monstrous Appearance just means it's easier to scare others and harder to seduce them. However, there's a reason that's a 0-pt. Flaw, so clans that previously suffered from an Appearance 0 weakness would need something else (choose an appropriate 4-pt. Flaw that fits). For the Gargoyle weakness, I'd go with Uncanny (4-pts).<br /> <br /> Since they also get Weak Willed (3-pts) and Amnesia (2-pts.), their weaknesses total about 9 points of Flaws. I'd offset that by giving them the equivalent of Petagia (4-pt. Merit, but worth less for Gargoyles) for free, even without Disciplines, and then I'd let Visceratika add flight on top of that to balance it out a bit. (I might let them trade Weak-Willed for Infertile Vitae or something.)<br /> <br /> Discipline-wise, I'd also rework the variants so they offer more variety:<br /> <br /> <b>Scout: </b>Auspex, Obfuscate and Visceratika<br /> <b>Sentinel: </b>Animalism, Fortitude, and Visceratika<br /> <b>Warrior:</b> Fortitude, Potence and Visceratika<br /> <br /> Otherwise, replacing Flight with Visceratika gives you Scouts with Auspex, Obfuscate and Visceratika (fine); Sentinels with Fortitude, Potence and Visceratika (okay, but it lacks a way to observe a domain beyond the bounds of the building itself); and Warriors with Fortitude, Protean and Visceratika (broken).<br /> <br /> Fortitude and Potence seem more like they'd fit the Warrior than the Sentinel. Giving Sentinels Animalism means they can use animals to act as spies and scouts across a domain, providing a variety of vantage points. It also means we've used all the Gangrel, Nosferatu and Tzimisce Disciplines except Protean and Vicissitude (which are essentially the source of Visceratika anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":".  Typo 10-17-2026, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-16T11:50:31-07:00","id":1564789,"title":"","content":"Reworking the Gargoyles is kind of a major story beat in my current chronicle where one of the PCs, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Erik_(Gangrel)\" target=\"_blank\">Erik</a>, that had his forced conversion in Gargoyle &quot;fixed&quot; during an encounter with a certain taxi driver in LA (the chronicle is sort of a mash up of the events in Bloodlines, Redemption and BJD, with some crypto-lore and homebrew events mixed in)<br /> <br /> Considering half the coterie are members of a noddist cabal connected with the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ankla_Hotep\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;False&quot; Caine</a> of Berlin, Erik fit in nicely and they have wondered through North America while half trying to track down the ancient's footsteps, half poking around whatever catches their fancy or an ally/mentor requests them to check into.<br /> <br /> And along the way they found out Erik's previous self had a warband of sorts, part of the Gargoyles are embroiled in a centuries-long civil/religious war centered around <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ferox\" target=\"_blank\">Ferox</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vukodlak\" target=\"_blank\">Vukodlak</a>, not to mention rumours of Erik's change have been making waves among both sides AND some of the Tremere.<br /> <br /> What only gets crazier as he starts to realize that whatever &quot;Caine&quot; did to him goes far beyond merely erasing the centuries of change, as he gets occasional memory flashes of his Gargoyle self, discovers he can turn back into Gargoyle as a warform so to speak - and can &quot;rewire&quot; other Gargoyles, doing to them like it was done unto him. (Sort of, but not quite)<br /> <br /> &quot;Undoing&quot; a Gargoyle - in the midst of the mayhem of an invasion of Elysium to boot - is the kind of juicy that has been <i><b>really </b></i>spreading like wildfire since.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-17T03:22:38-07:00","id":1564799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564144-house-ruling-gargoyles-v20?p=1564789#post1564789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reworking the Gargoyles is kind of a major story beat in my current chronicle where one of the PCs, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Erik_(Gangrel)\" target=\"_blank\">Erik</a>, that had his forced conversion in Gargoyle &quot;fixed&quot; during an encounter with a certain taxi driver in LA (the chronicle is sort of a mash up of the events in Bloodlines, Redemption and BJD, with some crypto-lore and homebrew events mixed in)<br /> <br /> Considering half the coterie are members of a noddist cabal connected with the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ankla_Hotep\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;False&quot; Caine</a> of Berlin, Erik fit in nicely and they have wondered through North America while half trying to track down the ancient's footsteps, half poking around whatever catches their fancy or an ally/mentor requests them to check into.<br /> <br /> And along the way they found out Erik's previous self had a warband of sorts, part of the Gargoyles are embroiled in a centuries-long civil/religious war centered around <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ferox\" target=\"_blank\">Ferox</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vukodlak\" target=\"_blank\">Vukodlak</a>, not to mention rumours of Erik's change have been making waves among both sides AND some of the Tremere.<br /> <br /> What only gets crazier as he starts to realize that whatever &quot;Caine&quot; did to him goes far beyond merely erasing the centuries of change, as he gets occasional memory flashes of his Gargoyle self, discovers he can turn back into Gargoyle as a warform so to speak - and can &quot;rewire&quot; other Gargoyles, doing to them like it was done unto him. (Sort of, but not quite)<br /> <br /> &quot;Undoing&quot; a Gargoyle - in the midst of the mayhem of an invasion of Elysium to boot - is the kind of juicy that has been <i><b>really </b></i>spreading like wildfire since.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you undid a gargoyle you should get three vampires, none who are the gargoyle. The gargoyle would be dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-17T05:49:38-07:00","id":1564801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564144-house-ruling-gargoyles-v20?p=1564799#post1564799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you undid a gargoyle you should get three vampires, none who are the gargoyle. The gargoyle would be dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite, for starters because Gargoyles are not Voltron or combiners from Transformers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, there's a bunch of confusion, back-&amp;-forth, retcons and unreliable narrators notes in the story of the process of Gargoyle-making - and in fact it might be, based upon these lore divergences, that there were multiple variants of the ritual during the centuries, each with their different requirements, pros and cons, until their abandonement with the Gargoyle revolt and the treaties during the formative decades of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Erik's transformation, specifically as portrayed in the events of Masquerade: Redemption, was something done to him only - no trio of vampires involving a Gangrel, Nosferatu and Tzimisce (walking into a bar) needed, for example. Anyway, much as he was changed back into a Gangrel, he has discovered that, under certain circunstances he can &quot;revert&quot; other kindred that were made into Gargoyles through such rituals back to their original clans, much like it was done to him, what has given <i>considerable </i>weight to his claims of being such a sort of individual.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Embraced </i></b>Gargoyles, now that is a different story, though they are not left unscatched by his newfound &quot;gift&quot; and he still has much to learn of the particulars of what the heck he's actually doing and how (it's a peculiar amalgam that &quot;Caine&quot; implanted in his memory while fixing the &quot;spaghetti code&quot; of blood done by the Tremere of yore).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-17-2026, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-17T07:36:22-07:00","id":1564802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564144-house-ruling-gargoyles-v20?p=1564801#post1564801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not quite, for starters because Gargoyles are not Voltron or combiners from Transformers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, there's a bunch of confusion, back-&amp;-forth, retcons and unreliable narrators notes in the story of the process of Gargoyle-making - and in fact it might be, based upon these lore divergences, that there were multiple variants of the ritual during the centuries, each with their different requirements, pros and cons, until their abandonement with the Gargoyle revolt and the treaties during the formative decades of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Erik's transformation, specifically as portrayed in the events of Masquerade: Redemption, was something done to him only - no trio of vampires involving a Gangrel, Nosferatu and Tzimisce (walking into a bar) needed, for example. Anyway, much as he was changed back into a Gangrel, he has discovered that, under certain circunstances he can &quot;revert&quot; other kindred that were made into Gargoyles through such rituals back to their original clans, much like it was done to him, what has given <i>considerable </i>weight to his claims of being such a sort of individual.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Embraced </i></b>Gargoyles, now that is a different story, though they are not left unscatched by his newfound &quot;gift&quot; and he still has much to learn of the particulars of what the heck he's actually doing and how (it's a peculiar amalgam that &quot;Caine&quot; implanted in his memory while fixing the &quot;spaghetti code&quot; of blood done by the Tremere of yore).</div> </div> </div> </div>Gargoyles are created from three vampires, and are in essence a new creature, or else they are embraced. What you're describing is a houserule in your group. You are free to do what you want, run nosferatu with appearance or say your venture are immune to the sun, but that's not how it works as a default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-17T15:18:56-07:00","id":1564808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564144-house-ruling-gargoyles-v20?p=1564802#post1564802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gargoyles are created from three vampires, and are in essence a new creature, or else they are embraced. What you're describing is a houserule in your group. You are free to do what you want, run nosferatu with appearance or say your venture are immune to the sun, but that's not how it works as a default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being the result of experiments with three clans and being individually the fusion of three vampires are two very different things.<br /> <br /> What you're describing isn't what's said in the books I've read. Maybe in the very first ones, but not assumed canon, then.<br /> <br /> Since Revised at least, the books are quite clear that a Gargoyle is one transformed mortal like any other vampire. They have amnesia, and they are an engineered Bloodline, but neither requires them to be anything different from one single transformed mortal.<br /> <br /> Your tone here was quite unnecessarily hostile. To begin with because, as Baaldam said, the books aren't always consistent and there are lots of places where radically different takes can still follow canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-18T04:59:10-07:00","id":1564820,"title":"","content":"The earliest rituals required three vampires, yes. But once they became a bloodline able to sire their own childer, it would be trivially easy to preserve some vitae to &quot;create&quot; more Gargoyles further down the line. Changing subjects who are already Kindred is naturally harder, but if the Baali and Ahrimanes can do it, then I'm sure the Tremere could figure it out, too.<br /> <br /> V20 confirms as much (they're not playable in V5, so this is the most recent info):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V20 CRB, p. 400</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gargoyles are created out of other Kindred, and this ugly fact makes their creation a seldom-discussed topic in polite vampiric society. The Tremere start with a Gangrel, Nosferatu, or Tzimisce vampire and perform obscene, bloody rituals using its blood, heart, and skin. <b>Vitae from </b><b>another vampire</b> (from <b>one of the other two </b><b>Clans</b>) is used to provoke a violent mutation, with the result that some Gargoyles look purely hideous (Nosferatu base), some look feral (Gangrel base), and some look fleshy and sport bony protrusions (Tzimisce base). No Gargoyle can pass for human.</div> </div> </div> </div>And:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V20 CRB, p. 401</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gargoyles creation rarely shows a discernible pattern. <b>The Change </b><b>tortures the new Gargoyle\u2019s body</b>, as bones elongate and split to form the wings. The face warps, leaving nothing to recognize <b>the mortal </b><b>or vampire</b> by. <b>They rarely remember their un</b><b>life or mortal existence</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, one subject, either mortal (by Embrace) or Kindred (by ritual), undergoes the Change, using Gargoyle vitae as normal for an Embrace or the blood of another clan if the subject is already a vampire. The Change splits their singular body, and they barely remember their life or unlife prior to the event. The use of single person thoughout (even when using they/them as a gender-neutral pronoun) indicates it only requires a single subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":".  Typo 10-18-2026, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-20T04:01:03-07:00","id":1564860,"title":"","content":"Especially early on things could get <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Hexaped\" target=\"_blank\">pretty</a> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Iecur\" target=\"_blank\">damn</a> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/List_of_Thaumaturgy_Rituals#ref_Furtitive_Integument\" target=\"_blank\">weird</a> about what a Gargoyle even is or not. It taps a bit into the mystery which property makes a bloodline or not, especially for created ones. My personal take tends to be that the bloodline gains &quot;identity&quot; that, metaphysically speaking, is strong enough to develop inherent characteristics. The Panders and their renaming ritual are a good example.<br /> <br /> That identity seems to be strong enough to even include individuals that are <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Rocia\" target=\"_blank\">outside</a> the usual scope, &quot;base components&quot; and &quot;ritual&quot; alone are not sufficient to make a bloodline. Even the Tremere themselves started with multiple individuals, so if it wasn't for that ephemeral unifying property they would be seven different Clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-20T04:34:33-07:00","id":1564862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564144-house-ruling-gargoyles-v20?p=1564860#post1564860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially early on things could get <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Hexaped\" target=\"_blank\">pretty</a> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Iecur\" target=\"_blank\">damn</a> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/List_of_Thaumaturgy_Rituals#ref_Furtitive_Integument\" target=\"_blank\">weird</a> about what a Gargoyle even is or not. It taps a bit into the mystery which property makes a bloodline or not, especially for created ones. My personal take tends to be that the bloodline gains &quot;identity&quot; that, metaphysically speaking, is strong enough to develop inherent characteristics. The Panders and their renaming ritual are a good example.<br /> <br /> That identity seems to be strong enough to even include individuals that are <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Rocia\" target=\"_blank\">outside</a> the usual scope, &quot;base components&quot; and &quot;ritual&quot; alone are not sufficient to make a bloodline. Even the Tremere themselves started with multiple individuals, so if it wasn't for that ephemeral unifying property they would be seven different Clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are, just with the same core spread.<br /> <br /> I think &quot;what makes a bloodline&quot; isn't the proper question, because the answer isn't actually metaphysical. You group vampires with similar characteristics and that's it, its a social concept.<br /> <br /> Same for clans or castes.<br /> <br /> What matters isn't this, but what makes a given flaw and Discipline spread inheritable.<br /> <br /> Bloodlines and Clans are usually defined by descent. You're Ventrue because you descend from [Ventrue]. You're Brujah because you descend from [Brujah]. Descending from a vampire makes you part of their line, that's just how the Curse works.<br /> <br /> Now, if you're Banu Haqim, you're a descendant of Haqim. BUT Haqim left three lineages. They are not interchangeable: you're Embraced into a Caste and that's the end of it. Mechanically it is indistinguishable from a Clan. The difference isn't an inherent distinction between what's a Caste and what's a Clan. It's that everyone knows the three lines come directly from Haqim and work together, so better treat as a single Clan.<br /> <br /> You sometimes have vampires with weird new weaknesses or a different Discipline spread for reasons. A Bloodline is usually what you call when this person Embraces and you find out their descendants inherit the change.<br /> <br /> Or maybe you don't even know where they come from, or they come from a known Ante, so they're technically a Clan or a Caste, but no one controls this. People call Bloodline or Clan or Caste whatever they feel like.<br /> <br /> Daughters of Cacophony, Samedi and Baali are all candidates to Clan status. They're Bloodlines just because proper society doesn't call them otherwise. Wu Zao and Nkulu Zao are considered Bloodlines, despite descending directly from Saulot.<br /> <br /> And Blood Brothers? They're worse than the Gargoyles, completely sterile, they're all made through ritual. The ritual is consistent and produces consistent results, that's the only reason they're called a Bloodline. Gargoyles, Tremere and Nagaraja are the same.<br /> <br /> Vampire does that on purpose. Characters act like there's an important metaphysical difference because they <i><b>believe</b></i>, and this belief is important to the game <i><b>because it has no evidence</b></i>. It may be right. It may not be. Outside that those are all made up distinctions and all you know metaphysically is that you inherit something from your Sire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-22T11:17:30-07:00","id":1564915,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Storytellers Handbook Revised has a whole section on what makes a bloodline or clan, and confirms it's mostly social. Kindred think you're a clan if you have or had an Antediluvian founder, and so long as they can fit you into the &quot;never more than 13&quot; schema.<br /> <br /> The Salubri technically had an Antediluvian founder (who's technically still alive), but they got replaced. There are legit Cappadocians still running around who also had one. But they aren't numerous enough and they'd have to off the Tremere or Giovanni first to claim their place.<br /> <br /> Several clans have a dead Antediluvian but still get classed as clans because of their size and influence. Others have a dead Antediluvian and were nearly decimated, but not enough time has passed for the intertia of considering them a clan to shift things (looking at you, Ravnos).<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that Tremere and Giovanni can claim to be the inheritors (or at least usurpers) of a particular clan in the first place. It's not just that they met the other criteria; they overtly supplanted another clan to take their status. If the Daughters of Cacophony managed to diablerise Arikel and decimate the Toreador, they might be able to lay claim to that clan's former mantle. Though they'd need to do some serious politicking to get the other clans to accept them as such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}